{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio.nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio.nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L240-L240","doc":"and it is the nonzero (bar-odd) amplitude a genuine A=3 lift forces\n(`A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_nonzero`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio.is_cross_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio.is_cross_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L237-L237","doc":"`E` is the frame-free cross-ratio of the global Birkhoff matrix — the gauge-invariant\nfunctional (`crossRatio_gauge_invariant`), not a single (gauge-dependent) entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio.mk","kind":"ctor","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L233-L233","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio","kind":"class","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L212-L240","doc":"**§3b dependent conjecture — the amplitude `E` is the GAUGE-INVARIANT cross-ratio of the global\nBirkhoff matrix, not a single (frame-dependent) entry.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (its content depends on the open construction of the global `0↔∞`\nBirkhoff connection matrix `P` of C1 — theta-valued, un-started;\n`docs/audits/2026-08-01-branch-selection-birkhoff-connection-matrix.md`, bean `qou-wiub`, the\nsibling's `BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean`).\n\nThe claim: the anti-self-adjoint amplitude `E` equals the **gauge-invariant** cross-ratio\n`crossRatio P₀₀ P₀₁ P₁₀ P₁₁` of the global Birkhoff matrix (frame-free, by\n`crossRatio_gauge_invariant`), and is nonzero (the bar-odd amplitude a genuine lift forces,\n`A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_nonzero`).  This is the **well-posed** target: it is NOT any\nsingle entry (`entry_not_gauge_invariant`), and the cross-ratio is the unique invariant\n(`gauge_fixes_all_iff`).\n\n**Content-bearing, not self-assuming.**  `is_cross_ratio` ties `E` to a SPECIFIC frame-free\nfunctional of the (open) matrix `P` — a falsifiable identification the sibling's construction\nmust satisfy, false for a generic assignment; `nonzero` is the forced bar-odd amplitude.  **No\ninstance is supplied**: building `P` and evaluating its cross-ratio is the open successor;\ndischarging this by *choosing* `crossRatio P` to hit `r*` (`amplitude_surjective`) would be the\nforbidden fit and is not done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.gauge_fixes_all_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.gauge_fixes_all_iff","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L176-L201","doc":"**The gauge fixes ALL four entries iff it is a global scale (sorry-free).**  With every entry\nnonzero, `P` is fixed by the gauge `(d_∞,0, d_∞,1, d_0,0, d_0,1)` iff\n`d_0,0 = d_∞,0`, `d_0,1 = d_∞,0`, and `d_∞,1 = d_∞,0` — i.e. all four normalisations are equal\n(the global scale `t·I`).  So the stabiliser of a generic `2×2` connection matrix is the\n1-parameter subgroup `K^×`; the gauge group `(K^×)⁴` acts with `4 − 1 = 3` effective scalar\nDOF on the four entries, leaving exactly `4 − 3 = 1` independent invariant — the cross-ratio.\nThis is the rigorous **dimension count** behind the well-posedness verdict. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.entry_not_gauge_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.entry_not_gauge_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L166-L172","doc":"**A nontrivial gauge genuinely moves a single entry (sorry-free).**  If the two\nnormalisations differ (`d_0 ≠ d_∞`) then the entry changes: `gaugeEntry d_∞ d_0 P ≠ P`.  A\nsingle entry is therefore NOT gauge-invariant — the direct contrapositive of\n`gaugeEntry_fix_iff`, exhibited as the (b) non-invariance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.gaugeEntry_fix_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.gaugeEntry_fix_iff","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L150-L164","doc":"**The gauge fixes an entry iff the two normalisations match on it (sorry-free).**  For a\nnonzero entry, `gaugeEntry d_∞ d_0 P = P ↔ d_0 = d_∞`.  The row/column normalisations must\ncoincide to leave the entry untouched — the atom of the stabiliser count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.entry_gauge_orbit_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.entry_gauge_orbit_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L140-L148","doc":"**A single off-diagonal entry carries a full elliptic-unit gauge freedom (sorry-free).**  For\nANY nonzero target unit `u` there is a genuine gauge (`d ≠ 0`) realising `P₀₁ ↦ u · P₀₁`\n(witness `d_∞,0 = 1`, `d_0,1 = u`).  So a single connection-matrix entry is defined only up to\nmultiplication by an arbitrary `q`-invariant (elliptic) unit: reading `E` off one entry is\n**ill-posed**, needing an extra normalisation datum to pin the gauge.  The residual freedom is\nthe whole multiplicative group of q-invariant units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.crossRatio_gauge_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.crossRatio_gauge_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L124-L136","doc":"**The cross-ratio is invariant under the full residual gauge (sorry-free).**  Under\n`P_{ij} ↦ (d_∞,i)⁻¹ P_{ij} d_0,j` the four gauge units `d_∞,0, d_∞,1, d_0,0, d_0,1` each cancel\nbetween numerator and denominator of `P₀₁·P₁₀/(P₀₀·P₁₁)`.  So the cross-ratio is a\n**frame-free** functional of the Birkhoff matrix — the well-posed target for reading `E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.crossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.crossRatio","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L117-L120","doc":"**The candidate frame-free functional: the cross-ratio** `P₀₁·P₁₀ / (P₀₀·P₁₁)`.  This is the\noff-diagonal-over-diagonal product ratio — the natural invariant of a `2×2` matrix under the\ndiagonal×diagonal gauge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.gaugeEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.gaugeEntry","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed.lean#L113-L115","doc":"**Gauge action on one connection-matrix entry.**  `d_∞,i` is the `∞`-side (row) normalisation,\n`d_0,j` the `0`-side (column) normalisation — both `q`-invariant (elliptic) units. ","signatureChunk":0}]}